      {
        "id": 132333,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-24T00:24:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That's a weird one. &nbsp;There's already a mechanism in place to handle what happens when a Limited card is put into play while a copy of it is already in play, so why layer on a restriction to the player's behavior to say that not only will it not work, <em>you can't even attempt it</em>. &nbsp;Doesn't the fact that it won't work cover the thing we're worried about, i.e. having multiple copies of the Limited card in play? &nbsp;I say, let 'em try it. &nbsp;Won't work anyway. &nbsp;Worst case, a player can try to seed their trash with extra copies of Limiteds they already have in play anyway.</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:07:48.074Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
