      {
        "id": 132337,
        "name": "Medic-Tank",
        "username": "Medic-Tank",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/{size}/2107_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-24T22:31:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's a weird one. &nbsp;There's already a mechanism in place to handle what happens when a Limited card is put into play while a copy of it is already in play, so why layer on a restriction to the player's behavior to say that not only will it not work, <em>you can't even attempt it</em>. &nbsp;Doesn't the fact that it won't work cover the thing we're worried about, i.e. having multiple copies of the Limited card in play? &nbsp;I say, let 'em try it. &nbsp;Won't work anyway. &nbsp;Worst case, a player can try to seed their trash with extra copies of Limiteds they already have in play anyway.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Perhaps so you can set up your limited equipment in the trash for recovery cards with rider effects. The only case I see this applying is La Capitan since she steals your stuff.</p>",
